  "description": "The integer-width premise. An integer token is judged by its TEXT against 2^53 = 9007199254740992, never by the double it would round to: a token within the 32-bit signed range reads as an integer (`int`); one beyond it and at most 2^53 in magnitude reads as a double, exactly (`float`, its binary64 bit pattern as 16 lower-case hex digits); one past 2^53 reads as a double only when it is that double's canonical float layout, and is otherwise refused (`refused`, the refusal's class). Each vector gives the `token`, read as a whole JSON document. A host reproduces every answer: its number type holds every integer up to 2^53 exactly, and it refuses the token 2^53 + 1 rather than reading it as 2^53.",
